<article class="env-proposition" id="0200">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0200">Proposition <span data-tag="0200">5.5.2.8</span>.</a> The coslice comparison functor $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{Kan}_{\ast } ) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{\ast }$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that, for every pair of pointed Kan complexes $(X,x)$ and $(Y,y)$, the evaluation map $\operatorname{Fun}(X,Y) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( \{ x\} , Y)$ is a Kan fibration (Corollary <a data-tag="00TM" href="/tag/00TM">3.1.3.3</a>). Proposition <a data-tag="0200" href="/tag/0200">5.5.2.8</a> is therefore a special case of Theorem <a data-tag="01ZS" href="/tag/01ZS">5.5.1.21</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
